{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++ code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <climits>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <functional>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing lint = long long;\nconst lint BIG = 1000000000000000000LL;\n\nint main() {\n#ifdef NEKROLM\n    freopen(\"input.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"output.txt\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    lint n;\n    cin >> n;\n    \n    vector<lint> dp(100000000, 0);\n    \n    function<lint(lint)> solve = [&](lint x) -> lint {\n        if (x == 0) return 0LL;\n        if (x < (lint)dp.size() && dp[x]) return dp[x];\n        \n        lint min_dist = BIG;\n        lint val = 1;\n        lint cnt = 0;\n        \n        while (abs(val - x) <= min_dist) {\n            min_dist = abs(val - x);\n            val = val * 10 + 1;\n            cnt++;\n        }\n        \n        val /= 10;\n        \n        if (val > x && val / 10) {\n            lint alt1 = cnt + solve(abs(val - x));\n            lint alt2 = (cnt - 1) + solve(abs(val / 10 - x));\n            if (x < (lint)dp.size()) return dp[x] = min(alt1, alt2);\n            return min(alt1, alt2);\n        }\n        \n        lint res = cnt + solve(abs(val - x));\n        if (x < (lint)dp.size()) return dp[x] = res;\n        return res;\n    };\n    \n    cout << solve(n);\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <climits>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <functional>\n#include <unordered_map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing lint = long long;\nconst lint BIG = 1000000000000000000LL;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    lint n;\n    cin >> n;\n    \n    unordered_map<lint, lint> memo;\n    \n    function<lint(lint)> solve = [&](lint x) -> lint {\n        if (x == 0) return 0LL;\n        if (x < 0) x = -x; // handle negative by taking absolute value\n        if (memo.find(x) != memo.end()) return memo[x];\n        \n        // Generate all numbers consisting of only 1s that are close to x\n        lint val = 1;\n        lint cnt = 1;\n        vector<pair<lint, lint>> candidates;\n        \n        // Generate numbers like 1, 11, 111, 1111, ... until they exceed x significantly\n        while (val <= x * 10) { // generate numbers up to 10x to be safe\n            candidates.push_back({val, cnt});\n            val = val * 10 + 1;\n            cnt++;\n        }\n        \n        lint min_ones = BIG;\n        \n        for (auto& [v, c] : candidates) {\n            // Option 1: use v (addend) and solve for x - v\n            if (v <= x) {\n                lint res = c + solve(x - v);\n                min_ones = min(min_ones, res);\n            }\n            // Option 2: use -v (subtract addend) and solve for x + v\n            // This is useful when v is slightly larger than x (like 111 for x=100)\n            lint diff = abs(v - x);\n            lint res = c + solve(diff);\n            min_ones = min(min_ones, res);\n        }\n        \n        return memo[x] = min_ones;\n    };\n    \n    cout << solve(n);\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.7\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00014876213390380144, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -0.00011836781777674332, 0.0, -2.50339189733495e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.22304809093475342, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -2.8967437174287625e-05, -2.5629668016335927e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0008044582791626453, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576272320060525e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.38920751214027405, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00023112009512260556, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -0.3492761552333832, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.003177833277732134, -0.0019424158381298184, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00015948931104503572, -7.807903602952138e-05, 0.0, -2.50339189733495e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.22541671991348267, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.3854863431770355e-05, -0.008740382269024849, -1.8000440832111053e-05, -8.022463589441031e-05, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -0.09294815361499786, -8.189342770492658e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -2.312633478140924e-05, -0.00010156115604331717, -0.00020466140995267779, -0.018198424950242043, -0.0007241725688800216, -7.784063927829266e-05, -0.00081815622979775